Description: SHADOW Arsenal profile - Web Application
 Scanners, fuzzers, proxies and TLS auditors for assessing web applications
 you own or are contracted to test. Includes content discovery, parameter
 mining, a SQL-injection tester, HTTP clients and transport-security checks.
 Several well-known web scanners (Burp Suite, OWASP ZAP, Nikto, Nuclei) are
 proprietary or not in Debian and are listed separately with official install
 links.
 .
 This metapackage depends on the 19 tools of the profile, all from Debian
 main; APT installs every one of them with it.
 .
 Not included, because they are not in Debian main: Burp Suite, OWASP ZAP,
 Nikto, Nuclei, feroxbuster, DirBuster, Dalfox, XSStrike, Commix, Ghauri,
 Jaeles, Kiterunner, Skipfish, Wapiti, Arachni, retire.js, Wappalyzer, WPScan.
 The Arsenal manager lists where their vendors publish them.
 .
 These tools are for authorised security testing, research, defence and
 education only: use them on systems you own or have explicit written
 permission to test, and follow the law that applies to you. They come with no
 warranty.

