Description: SHADOW Arsenal profile - Red Team
 Credential attacks, exploitation helpers, Active Directory and Windows
 protocol tooling, and pivoting utilities for engagements you have written
 authorization to perform. Several cornerstone frameworks (Metasploit,
 Responder, NetExec, BloodHound, Sliver) are not in Debian main and are listed
 as external tools with vendor install instructions rather than bundled.
 .
 This metapackage depends on the 37 tools of the profile, all from Debian
 main; APT installs every one of them with it.
 .
 Not included, because they are not in Debian main: Metasploit Framework,
 NetExec, Evil-WinRM, Responder, BloodHound, Sliver, Exploit-DB
 (searchsploit), RouterSploit, pwncat, Ropper, enum4linux-ng, CrackMapExec,
 Certipy, Kerbrute, PingCastle, BloodHound.py, Social-Engineer Toolkit (SET),
 Gophish, King Phisher, Evilginx, Modlishka, BeEF, airgeddon, Wifiphisher,
 Fern Wifi Cracker, Kismet. The Arsenal manager lists where their vendors
 publish them.
 .
 These tools are for authorised security testing, research, defence and
 education only: use them on systems you own or have explicit written
 permission to test, and follow the law that applies to you. They come with no
 warranty.

